### Configure Prisma connection in prisma.config.ts

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/blog/content/blog/testing-series-1-8eRB5p0Y8o/index.mdx

Uses defineConfig to point to the schema and provide the database URL. Explicitly imports dotenv/config as Prisma 7 does not load .env files automatically.

```ts
// prisma.config.ts
import 'dotenv/config'
import { defineConfig } from 'prisma/config'

export default defineConfig({
  schema: 'prisma/schema.prisma',
  datasource: {
    url: process.env.DATABASE_URL!
  }
})
```

--------------------------------

### prisma.config.ts

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/core-concepts/supported-databases/sqlite.mdx

Set the connection URL in prisma.config.ts.

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from "prisma/config";

export default defineConfig({
  schema: "prisma/schema.prisma",
  datasource: {
    url: "file:./dev.db", // or libsql:// for Turso
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Prisma ORM 7 with prisma.config.ts

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/blog/content/blog/advanced-database-schema-management-with-atlas-and-prisma-orm/index.mdx

Define the schema path, migrations directory, and datasource URL. Ensure the DATABASE_URL environment variable is set so the configuration can resolve it.

```typescript
// prisma.config.ts
import "dotenv/config";
import { defineConfig, env } from "prisma/config";

export default defineConfig({
  schema: "prisma/schema.prisma",
  migrations: {
    path: "prisma/migrations",
  },
  datasource: {
    url: env("DATABASE_URL"),
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Instantiate Prisma Client with SQLite Adapter

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/blog/content/blog/try-the-new-rust-free-version-of-prisma-orm-early-access/index.mdx

Initialize `PrismaClient` by passing an instance of `PrismaBetterSQLite3` as the adapter, connecting to a SQLite database.

```ts
import { PrismaBetterSQLite3 } from '@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3';
import { PrismaClient } from './generated/prisma';

const adapter = new PrismaBetterSQLite3({ url: process.env.DATABASE_URL })
const prisma = new PrismaClient({ adapter });
```

--------------------------------

### Initialize Prisma Client with better-sqlite3 Driver Adapter

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/site/content/changelog/2025-05-01.mdx

Use the @prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3 package to interact with SQLite databases in a JS-native way.

```typescript
import { PrismaBetterSQLite3 } from '@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3';
import { PrismaClient } from './generated/prisma';

const adapter = new PrismaBetterSQLite3({
  url: "file:./prisma/dev.db"
});
const prisma = new PrismaClient({ adapter });
```

