Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/blog/content/blog/advanced-database-schema-management-with-atlas-and-prisma-orm/index.mdx

Define the schema path, migrations directory, and datasource URL. Ensure the DATABASE_URL environment variable is set so the configuration can resolve it.

```typescript
// prisma.config.ts
import "dotenv/config";
import { defineConfig, env } from "prisma/config";

export default defineConfig({
  schema: "prisma/schema.prisma",
  migrations: {
    path: "prisma/migrations",
  },
  datasource: {
    url: env("DATABASE_URL"),
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Instantiate Prisma Client with SQLite Adapter

Source: https://github.com/prisma/web/blob/main/apps/blog/content/blog/try-the-new-rust-free-version-of-prisma-orm-early-access/index.mdx

Initialize `PrismaClient` by passing an instance of `PrismaBetterSQLite3` as the adapter, connecting to a SQLite database.

```ts
import { PrismaBetterSQLite3 } from '@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3';
import { PrismaClient } from './generated/prisma';

const adapter = new PrismaBetterSQLite3({ url: process.env.DATABASE_URL })
const prisma = new PrismaClient({ adapter });
```

